  "final_text": "All four steps are done. The rule reads back as enabled.\n\n- **Data view:** 'Kibana Sample Data Logs' has the time field `timestamp`. The response code field is `response` (string), with `response.keyword` for exact matching.\n- **Dashboard:** 'S4-10b9a621 Web logs' (id `s4-10b9a621-web-logs-be8b349b1afa`) has two panels: \"Requests over time\" (count, date histogram on `timestamp`, line chart) and \"Requests by HTTP response code\" (count by `response.keyword`, bar chart).\n- **Alert rule:** 'S4-10b9a621 5xx errors' (id `75162fac-47ca-4d93-9ca7-55cc96fdfe6c`) is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, running every 1m. It fires when the count of documents with `response.keyword` from \"500\" to \"599\" in the last 5 minutes is greater than 10. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Panel edit:** The response-code panel is now titled \"Responses by code\". The dashboard shows the new title.\n\nChoices I made:\n- The 5xx filter uses a string range on `response.keyword`. This is exact for three-digit codes but would not be correct for non-numeric values.\n- I used a bar chart for the response-code panel and a line chart for requests over time.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
